    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter August 24th with a clear priority on speed and high-leverage spots, headlined by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98), who is our elite play of the day. Facing Merrill Kelly (5.27 xERA), **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from a massive SP skill boost and an optimized leadoff role, making him the cornerstone of our lineup. **Junior Caminero** (70.50) also earns a strong start despite a tough matchup against Framber Valdez, as his position in the three-hole and park-adjusted projection outweigh the traditional platoon disadvantage for a right-handed hitter. Meanwhile, **Lars Nootbaar** (58.28) provides solid value, buoyed by a significant dynamic platoon edge that keeps him above the marginal threshold despite facing Kevin Gausman.\n\nThe margins remain tight for **Colt Keith** (51.15), **Trea Turner** (52.32), and **Kyle Schwarber** (51.53), all of whom are effectively \"starts by necessity\" given their top-of-the-order roles. We are consciously managing the floor today; **Dillon Dingler** (35.83) was our most notable exclusion, falling well short of our 40.0 efficiency threshold. While **Dillon Dingler** offers some park-factor upside against Rasmussen, the combination of a high SP skill penalty and a significant platoon disadvantage against a right-handed starter made him an easy bench decision to preserve our limited game caps. \n\nRisk management remains a theme as we navigate high-skill opposing arms. **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber** face a stiff challenge in Logan Gilbert, whose 3.46 xERA suppresses their raw output significantly. We are keeping a close watch on **Chase Meidroth** (46.14) and **Caleb Durbin** (55.78); while neither is a standout, their availability ensures we maintain roster depth without overextending our daily cap. With **Christian Yelich**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, and **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** all inactive today, the pressure is on the active core to maximize these plate appearances against a mix of mid-tier and elite pitching.",
